.TH CMUXR-FLOOR 1 "2026-10-20" "cmuxr" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cmuxr-floor \- show an audio-reactive floor in an OpenXR session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cmuxr-floor
.RB [ "\-\-size WIDTHxDEPTH" ]
.RB [ "\-\-server URL" ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-player ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cmuxr-floor
uses the active DomeD XR session when DomeD is running.
If DomeD has no active XR session, it starts the renderer attached to DomeD's
control service. A standalone OpenXR overlay alongside the current WiVRn
application is used only when DomeD is not in use.
If DomeD is present but its control service is unavailable, startup reports an
error instead of falling back. A standalone overlay yields to DomeD when it starts.
It enables the floor preference and starts the cmuxr tray player if no engine
is available and a graphical session is present.
Select a track and start playback in the player to animate the floor.
.PP
The effect uses sixteen frequency bands from the player's decoded audio.
A sixteen-by-sixteen grid of coloured tiles is anchored five millimetres above
the OpenXR STAGE floor. It captures neither microphone nor unrelated system audio.
The overlay does not receive pointer input.
Only one instance of this launcher runs per user runtime directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-size " WIDTHxDEPTH
Set floor width and depth in metres. Each dimension must be finite,
greater than zero and at most 100. The chosen extent is saved as floor_size_m in the frontend settings and is
also respected by the integrated DomeD renderer. The alias
.B \-\-floor-size
is also accepted. Without this option, use the runtime's STAGE bounds.
Height and anchoring always use STAGE.
.TP
.BI "\-\-server " URL
Select the DomeD control service. The URL must be http://127.0.0.1:PORT.
An explicit server disables standalone fallback.
Otherwise DOME_PREVIEW_PORT selects the port, defaulting to 49640.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-player
Do not start a tray player automatically. Use an already-running GUI or console engine.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.SH RUNTIME REQUIREMENTS
An active OpenXR runtime, Vulkan, and a valid STAGE reference space are required.
The renderer prefers XR_EXTX_overlay and transparent alpha or additive blending.
It does not replace the main application's scene with an opaque background.
.PP
Some WiVRn builds return XRT_ERROR_NOT_IMPLEMENTED when queried for room bounds.
Use an explicit size in that case. LOCAL space is never assumed to be a floor.
The application-menu launcher uses an explicit 3 by 3 metre extent.
.PP
The effect disappears when disabled, paused, stopped, or when spectrum data is
more than 500 milliseconds old. The renderer can remain running with no visible
floor while playback is stopped. It requires one additional composition layer.
.SH INSTALLATION
The optional renderer is built from a compatible DomeD checkout with the supplied
music-floor integration patch. To stage the system application and renderer:
.nf
CMUXR_WITH_XR=1 CMUXR_DOMED_SOURCE=../DomeD \
  DESTDIR="$PWD/stage" ./scripts/install-cmuxr.sh /usr/local
.fi
.PP
Install the staged tree with administrator privileges after reviewing it.
The player, frontend and manual pages can be installed without the XR component.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DOME_PREVIEW_PORT
Select the local DomeD control port, defaulting to 49640.
.TP
.B XR_RUNTIME_JSON
Override the OpenXR runtime manifest for this process.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Directory containing cmuxr-floor.json and the launcher instance lock.
.TP
.B CMUS_SOCKET
Override the player control socket used to detect a running engine.
.SH CONTROL
Pause the player to suspend the visible floor.
Run
.B cmuxr --floor off
to disable it persistently, or use the tray switch.
Interrupt the renderer with Ctrl+C when it was started from a terminal.
The currently running WiVRn session remains active.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cmuxr-floor --size 3x3
cmuxr-floor --no-player --size 4x2.5
cmuxr --floor off
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cmuxr (1),
.BR cmus (1)
